  "paragraph": 33,
  "text": "Even better, run a two-by-two evaluation matrix comparing old and new models against old and new harnesses. This single habit prevents one of the sneakiest traps in AI engineering. A clever scaffold or strict workflow rule that rescued last year's weaker model often throttles this year's frontier model by boxing in its reasoning. Measuring both axes regularly shows whether your gains came from the model or the harness, and reveals the exact moment when stripping away old constraints unlocks a major jump in performance.",
